This wake closed three seed-43 cells and launched the last three grid cells. The answer to the length question on page images is still open; it needs the seed-43 runs at 20 and 40 pages, which are running. Nothing is needed from you.

## Done
- **Three seed-43 cells passed their health checks.** These are the compressed model R on text, on 10 pages, and on 10 mixed items (pages as images plus pages as text). Every row was judged, the answer-length cap was hit 1–4% of the time (limit 5%), and the number of compressed slots matched the prediction exactly. All three are closed in the ledger.
- **Seed 43 repeats seed 42.** The compressed reader scores well below the uncompressed one, on the same questions:

| set | compressed judge accuracy ↑ (seed 43) | uncompressed judge accuracy ↑ | gap, seed 43 (95% CI) | gap, seed 42 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| text, 2,246 questions | .422 | .594 | −17.3 pt [−19.4, −15.1] | −17.9 pt |
| 10 pages, 1,407 questions | .489 | .672 | −18.3 pt [−21.3, −15.4] | −16.6 pt |
| 10 mixed items, 1,407 questions | .459 | .654 | −19.5 pt [−22.3, −16.5] | −20.5 pt |

- **The length test cannot decide on text with this set.** The length test asks whether the gap grows on longer documents (~8k / ~16k / ~32k tokens against ~4k). The change in the gap was −2.5 / −0.7 / −1.7 pt at seed 43, and +0.7 / +3.6 / +3.9 pt at seed 42.
  - No seed shows a loss.
  - The campaign's rule for "no length loss" needs the 95% range to stay inside ±3 pt. With only 411–637 questions per length group, the range is ±4 to ±6 pt, so the rule cannot be met.

## Launched (3 of the 4 allowed per wake)
- **Long-chunk training on text, seed 43.** This is a pair of models: one whose first training stage used 1,024-token chunks, and one that used 256-token chunks. Both are evaluated on the long-document text set.
- **The no-document baseline, run again.** This baseline asks the uncompressed model the questions without the document. The first run used an older version of `pisco/model.py`, so the campaign rule did not let it count as a fair comparison. Setting `CML=1024` only changes the output file name; that setting is not used in this mode.
- The fourth slot is saved for one re-scoring job with the second judge prompt. It waits until the 40-page seed-43 run is in.

## Running now
Nine cells:
- the compressed model at seed 43 on 20 and 40 pages, and on 20 and 40 mixed items;
- the long-chunk text pairs at seeds 42 and 43;
- the no-document baseline.

They should all end between about 05:05 and 08:00. The next wake then decides:
- whether the page-image gap grows with length (seed 42 alone: −6.5 pt from 10 to 40 pages);
- whether long-chunk training helps or hurts on long text.

## Budget
- Cells: 84 of 87 used.
- GPU-hours: about 73 of 114 used, and about 90 expected at the end.

I updated `docs/longdoc_diagnosis.md`, `STATE.md` and the display page. I added a +1 to an existing expmon complaint: the campaign's GPU-hours still have to be summed by hand.
